# Renvor — repository ignore rules
#
# Scope: spec FR-024 requires that a full verification run on a clean checkout leaves
# no untracked or modified files. Exclusions decided at T009 are enforced here.
#
# NOTE: these rules prevent FUTURE commits only. Material already committed is not
# removed by ignoring it — see the pre-push blocker in governance/phase-001-evidence.md.

# --- Rust build output ---
target/
debug/
**/*.rs.bk
*.rlib
*.prof*

# --- Node and documentation site output ---
node_modules/
.docusaurus/
build/
.cache/
docs/build/

# --- Editor and IDE state ---
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo

# --- Operating-system artifacts ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Logs and temporary files ---
*.log
tmp/
*.tmp

# --- Environment, credentials, and secrets (never commit) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials
credentials.*
secrets/
*.secret

# --- Python (local tooling only) ---
.venv/
__pycache__/

# --- Local agent and development-tool configuration ---
# Restored to the TRACKED ignore file on 2026-08-19, after two independent automated review
# passes flagged its removal.
#
# These were moved to `.git/info/exclude` on the reasoning that local-only material does not
# belong in a rule imposed on everyone who clones. That reasoning does not survive contact with
# two facts: this repository is **public**, and `.git/info/exclude` is **per-clone**. A second
# clone — another machine, another contributor, CI — inherits none of it, and a single broad
# `git add .` there publishes local tool state irreversibly. A published secret is not
# retractable, and this file is the only protection that travels with the repository.
#
# `.git/info/exclude` keeps them too. This is belt and braces, deliberately.
.claude/
.claude-flow/
.playwright-mcp/
.remember/
.specify/

# --- Separately managed brand package, separate asset licensing (T009) ---
Branding/

# --- Superseded planning documents, retained locally as research references (T009) ---
RENVOR_FRAMEWORK_DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md
RENVOR_MASTER_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
